 1. now  RUBY_VERSION >= "4.0"                    true   (major 4)
 2. 2.0  keyword arguments, Module#prepend        def f(a:, b: 2) compiles: true   prepend: true
 3. 2.1  refinements                              Refinement class: true
 4. 2.3  &. safe navigation, Hash#dig             nil&.length compiles: true   dig: true
 5. 2.4  one Integer class                        Fixnum defined: false   1.class: Integer   (2**100).class: Integer
 6. 2.5  rescue inside do...end blocks            compiles: true
 7. 2.6  endless range, then, proc >>             (1..) compiles: true   then: true   >>: true
 8. 2.7  pattern matching, ... forwarding, _1     case/in: true   (...): true   _1: true
 9. 3.0  keyword separation, Ractor, endless def  f({a: 1}) no longer fills **opts: true   Ractor: true   def f = 1: true
10. 3.1  {x:} shorthand, Class#subclasses         compiles: true   subclasses: true
11. 3.2  Data, anonymous * ** &, linear_time?     Data.define: true   def f(*, **, &) = g(*, **, &): true   Regexp.linear_time?: true
12. 3.3  Prism parser ships with Ruby             require "prism" then Prism defined: true
13. 3.4  it, chilled literals, 'name' quoting     [1].map { it }: true   "a".frozen?: false (chilled, not frozen)   message: "undefined method 'foo' for nil"
14. 4.0  core Set, Ractor::Port, ZJIT, Ruby::Box  Set needs no require and is C code: true   Ractor::Port: true   RubyVM::ZJIT: true   Ruby::Box: true
15. 4.0  Warning.categories                       [:deprecated, :experimental, :performance, :strict_unused_block]
